Subject: [PATCH] Use the normal hostapd association comeback interval type

The HAL initializes hostapd BSS configuration itself. With testing options
compiled in, leaving test_assoc_comeback_type zero silently overrides the
normal association-comeback type with reserved type zero. Returning PMF
stations then ignore the comeback interval and blacklist the target BSS
instead of retrying after SA Query. Match hostapd's default sentinel without
disabling PMF, shortening the SA Query timeout or bypassing authentication.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/wifi_hal_hostapd.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_hostapd.c
@@ -241,6 +241,9 @@
     conf->assoc_sa_query_max_timeout = 1000;
     conf->assoc_sa_query_retry_timeout = 201;
     conf->group_mgmt_cipher = WPA_CIPHER_AES_128_CMAC;
+#ifdef CONFIG_TESTING_OPTIONS
+    conf->test_assoc_comeback_type = -1;
+#endif
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211W */
 #ifdef EAP_SERVER_FAST
 //Defined
